<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42448" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sămărīa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σαμάρεια</span> (orig. Heb. ), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the middle district of
			Palestine</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 13, 14, §
			68</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Să-mărītae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Samaria</i>, <i>the
			Samaritans</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 12, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 4 Reg.
				17, 29</span></i>.—In sing.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sămărī-tes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>a Samaritan</i>,
			Hadr. ap. <i><span class="en">Vop. Sat.
			8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sămărītis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>a
				Samaritan woman</i>, <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 2,
			246</span></i>; <i><span class="en">252</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Alcim. 3,
			405</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sămărītānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Samaritan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">via,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sedul. 4, 222</span></i>
			.—In plur., <i>the
				Samaritans</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2</span></i> Esd. 4,
			2.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sămărītĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Samaritan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 2, 256</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sămă-rēus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Samaritan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">superstitio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 3, 45</span></i>
			.</div>
